{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1094", "sample_idx": 41, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "```json\n{\n  \"famous_moms_with_attitude\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Beyoncé Giselle Knowles-Carter (aka Queen Bey, aka 'Who ran the world? GIRL!')\",\n      \"claim_to_fame\": \"Pop princess, X-factor phenom, and the mom who raised Blue Ivy while still dropping albums with more swagger than a runway in Milan. Also, her parenting Instagram is *chef's kiss*.\",\n      \"random_fact\": \"She once scolded a reporter for asking about her kids in an interview like they were 'just another topic.' Icon move.\",\n      \"mom_energy\": \"‘I woke up like this... and then I also woke up to nursery school drop-off. Still iconic.’\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Oprah Winfrey (aka The Oracle of Omelettes & Empowerment)\",\n      \"claim_to_fame\": \"The queen of talk shows, book clubs, and *infomercial-worthy* life advice. Raised a household of 10+ kids (birth and chosen) while building an empire. Also, she once cried on national TV for like three seasons—mom goals.\",\n      \"random_fact\": \"She gave away *millions* of cars via her show, but her kids? They got the emotional support vehicles (aka her undivided attention).\",\n      \"mom_energy\": \"‘You get a car! *And* you get a car! *And* you get emotional growth!’ (Applause.)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Mère Teresa (aka The Saint Who Smelled Like Humility and Baby Powder)\",\n      \"claim_to_fame\": \"Founded the Missionaries of Charity, raised *thousands* of spiritual kids, and had a knack for hugging people *way* harder than most moms dare. Also, her ‘little flowers’ (aka orphaned kids) grew up to believe in miracles.\",\n      \"random_fact\": \"She once wrote letters to her ‘spiritual children’ like they were her actual kids. *Creepy?* Or just holy? You decide.\",\n      \"mom_energy\": \"‘Come to me, all ye who are burdened, and I will give you nap time... in heaven.’\"\n    